      "solution": "n = int(input())\narr = list(map(int, input().split()))\n\ndp = [1] * n\n\nfor i in range(n):\n    for j in range(i):\n        if arr[j] < arr[i]:\n            dp[i] = max(dp[i], dp[j] + 1)\n\nprint(max(dp))",
      "statement": "You are given a sequence of integers.\nYour task is to determine the length of the longest strictly increasing subsequence.\n\nA subsequence is obtained by removing zero or more elements without changing the order of the remaining ones.\n\nExample:\nFor the sequence [[3 1 2 5 4]], the longest increasing subsequence is [[1 2 5]], so the answer is [[3]].",
